cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenSmell in your work, please cite this software."
title: "OpenSmell"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vranesi"
    given-names: "Cyril"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-02"
url: "https://github.com/YAAASSS/OpenSmell"
repository-code: "https://github.com/YAAASSS/OpenSmell"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  OpenSmell is an experimental open interoperability layer for representing,
  connecting, exchanging, validating, and rendering heterogeneous digital
  olfaction information across datasets, software, scientific models, and
  devices. It does not define how odors must be physically reproduced.
keywords:
  - "digital olfaction"
  - "olfaction"
  - "interoperability"
  - "odor representation"
  - "scent display"
  - "sensory data"
